<article class="env-lemma" id="068T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/068T">Lemma <span data-tag="068T">15.76.13</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $K^\bullet $ be a complex of $R$-modules. Let $R \to R'$ be a faithfully flat ring map. If the complex $K^\bullet \otimes _ R R'$ is perfect, then $K^\bullet $ is perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Lemma <a href="/tag/0658" data-tag="0658">15.76.2</a> this translates into the corresponding results for pseudo-coherent modules and modules of finite tor dimension. See Lemma <a href="/tag/068S" data-tag="068S">15.68.17</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/068R" data-tag="068R">15.66.15</a> for those results. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>